{"availability":"available","full":"SharedCode/joltrin","name":"joltrin","description":"Durable memory and a verification barrier for AI agents, in one embedded Go library.","category":"Developer tools","language":"Go","stars":25,"forks":5,"created":"2015-04-04T08:22:47Z","updated":"2026-10-06T06:45:01Z","license":"MIT","branch":"master","homepage":"https://joltrinhq.com","topics":["acid-transactions","ai-agents","b-tree","cicd","database","distributed-systems","embedded-database","erasure-coding","golang","release-automation","scalable","vector-search","webassembly"],"demo":"https://joltrinhq.com/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-06T15:42:53.638Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-06T15:42:53.638Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-06T15:42:53.638Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-04T08:15:41.051Z","stars":25,"forks":5},{"at":"2026-10-06T15:42:53.638Z","stars":25,"forks":5}],"technologies":["Go"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Durable memory and a verification barrier for AI agents, in one embedded Go library.","joltrinhq.com · Technical demo · Arena · Agent barrier","Joltrin (formerly SOP) is an ACID-compliant B-Tree storage engine that runs inside your process. For AI agents it provides three things in one library: memory that survives a crash and can be resumed by another worker, vector search stored next to structured data in the same transaction, and a verification barrier that blocks a risky action until its preconditions are proven."],"features":["Latency. About 6.9 microseconds per B-Tree write or read, over 140,000 ops/sec with WAL logging, from the repo's own harness on a 2015 dual-core MacBook Pro. Reproduce it with go run ./tools/benchmark. Details and…","Correctness. The race detector runs on the core engine packages in CI, govulncheck runs on every push, and the build and unit tests run on Linux, macOS, and Windows.","Packages. Published on PyPI (sop4py) and NuGet (Sop), plus the Go module."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.co